<div class="article-detail-page">
    <div class="article-body">

        <p>Shipping on Lively is designed to be simple, but there are a few important steps you'll need to take along the way.</p>
        <p>Use this checklist to understand how to manage shipping before and after you make a sale.</p>
        <p>This page covers key tasks that help you ship confidently, keep buyers happy, and get paid:</p>

        <ol>
            <li><a href="#setup">Set up shipping before you sell</a></li>
            <li><a href="#review">Review your orders after a sale</a></li>
            <li><a href="#labels">Create and print shipping labels</a></li>
            <li><a href="#pack">Pack your orders</a></li>
            <li><a href="#ship">Ship your orders</a></li>
            <li><a href="#paid">Get paid</a></li>
        </ol>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="setup">1. Set up shipping before you sell</h2>

        <p>Take a few minutes to review your shipping setup before you go live and start selling:</p>

        <p>☐ <a href="#">Review your shipping settings.</a></p>
        <p>☐ <strong>Enter accurate item weights when creating listings</strong>, including the item and all packaging materials.</p>

        <p><strong>Why this matters:</strong> By default, buyers pay for shipping at checkout. Your shipping settings and item weights help determine those costs, so keeping them accurate helps avoid surprises for both you and your buyers.</p>

        <p><strong>Learn more</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#">Setting up shipping before you sell</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">Choose shipping profiles for your products</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">Edit your shipping settings</a></li>
        </ul>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="review">2. Review your orders after a sale</h2>

        <p>After you make a sale, take a quick look at your <strong>Shipments</strong> in Seller Hub:</p>

        <p>☐ <strong>Check for cancellation requests.</strong> If you plan to ship the orders, <a href="#">decline any requests</a> before generating labels.</p>
        <p>☐ <strong>Review automatically bundled orders,</strong> and <a href="#">bundle or unbundle</a> shipments if needed.</p>
        <p>☐ <strong>Update shipment weights or dimensions</strong> if they don't match the package you're sending.</p>

        <p><strong>Why this matters:</strong> A quick review now can help you catch issues and make sure your labels are accurate. It's much easier to make changes before labels are created.</p>

        <p><strong>Learn more</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#">Pack and ship your orders</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">Edit shipments after a sale</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">Accept or decline cancellation requests</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">Bundle or unbundle shipments</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">How Smart Bundling™ works</a></li>
        </ul>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="labels">3. Create and print shipping labels</h2>

        <p>When you're ready to generate shipping labels:</p>

        <p>☐ Use a <strong>desktop browser</strong> and make sure you have <strong>access to a printer.</strong></p>
        <p>☐ <a href="#">Confirm your return address and label format.</a></p>
        <p>☐ <a href="#">Generate prepaid labels and packing slips.</a></p>

        <p><strong>Good to know:</strong> Packing slips are optional, but they can make packing easier and help buyers identify their orders when they arrive.</p>

        <p><strong>Learn more</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#">Update your default shipping label settings (size, return address)</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">Generate and print shipping labels</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">Change or fix your shipping label</a></li>
        </ul>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="pack">4. Pack your orders</h2>

        <p>To prepare your shipments for transit:</p>

        <p>☐ <strong>Package items securely</strong> for transit.</p>
        <p>☐ <strong>Include the packing slip</strong> and a thank you note (optional).</p>
        <p>☐ <strong>Attach the shipping label</strong> securely to the package.</p>

        <p><strong>Why this matters:</strong> Secure packaging helps protect items in transit and can reduce the risk of delivery issues, damage claims, and refund requests.</p>

        <p><strong>Learn more</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#">Packaging guidelines</a></li>
        </ul>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="ship">5. Ship your orders</h2>

        <p>☐ <strong>Drop off packages</strong> with the carrier within <strong>2 business days of the sale.</strong></p>

        <p><strong>Good to know:</strong> You don't need to wait for a carrier scan to show you've shipped on time. Before drop-off, <a href="#">scan your packages in the app</a> to instantly share proof of shipment and notify buyers that their orders are on the way, complete with a photo of the package.</p>

        <p><strong>Learn more</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#">Confirm drop-off with the in-app scanner</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">Shipping policy for sellers</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">Shipping guides by country</a></li>
        </ul>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="paid">6. Get paid</h2>

        <p>☐ <strong>Wait for your earnings to become available</strong> in your Lively <a href="#">account balance.</a></p>
        <p>☐ <a href="#"><strong>Start a payout</strong></a> to transfer funds to your bank account.</p>

        <p><strong>Good to know:</strong> Until you qualify for Early Payout, your earnings typically begin processing after the carrier confirms delivery. You can track <a href="#">shipment status in Seller Hub</a>, and <a href="#">monitor your Lively balance</a> to see when earnings are processing or available for payout.</p>

        <p><strong>Learn more</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#">When you'll get paid on Lively</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">Start a payout</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">Track your earnings and payout status</a></li>
        </ul>

